#exam-pointer(title: "HIGH-YIELD MEMORY HOOKS & HISTORIOGRAPHICAL POINTERS")[
  - *Deterrence vs Defense:* Deterrence *prevents* war; defense *fights and limits damage* once war begins.
  - *BWC Treaty Date:* Signed in *1972*; completely banned biological weapons.
  - *CWC Treaty Date:* Concluded in *1992*; opened in Paris in 1993; verifiably destroys chemical weapons via OPCW.
  - *NPT Cutoff Date:* *1 January 1967*; recognized only the 5 permanent states; rejected by India as discriminatory.
  - *ABM Treaty:* Signed in *1972* by US and USSR; restricted anti-ballistic missile shields; US withdrew in 2002.
  - *Human Security Referent:* Shifts focus from sovereign state territory to *individual human beings and communities*.
  - *Narrow vs Broad Human Security:* Narrow = "Freedom from Fear" (violence); Broad = "Freedom from Want" (hunger/disease).
  - *Refugee vs IDP:* Refugees cross an *international border*; IDPs remain *within their own country* (e.g., Kashmiri Pandits).
  - *Non-Refoulement:* International legal rule prohibiting expulsion of refugees back to danger.
  - *Pokhran Tests:* Pokhran-I in *May 1974*; Pokhran-II in *May 1998*; doctrine is *Credible Minimum Deterrence & No First Use*.
]

