#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (Deterrence vs Defense):* Deterrence aims to *prevent* war from occurring; defense aims to *limit damage and defeat* the enemy once war has started.
  2. *Trap 2 (BWC vs CWC Dates):* BWC was signed in *1972* (biological); CWC was concluded in *1992* (chemical). Do not swap these years!
  3. *Trap 3 (NPT Arbitrary Cutoff Date):* The NPT cutoff date is *1 January 1967*, NOT 15 August 1947 or May 1974.
  4. *Trap 4 (Refugees vs IDPs):* Refugees must cross an *international border*; individuals displaced within their own country (such as Kashmiri Pandits) are *Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs)*.
  5. *Trap 5 (Narrow vs Broad Human Security):* Narrow conception focuses strictly on *violence and fear*; broad conception includes *hunger, disease, and economic want*.
  6. *Trap 6 (Pokhran-I vs Pokhran-II Dates):* Pokhran-I occurred in *May 1974* (Indira Gandhi); Pokhran-II occurred in *May 1998* (Atal Bihari Vajpayee).
  7. *Trap 7 (India's Alliances):* India has *never* joined formal military alliances like NATO or Warsaw Pact; India pursued strategic autonomy through Non-Alignment (NAM).
]

